#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION Orchestration"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Declared jobs with bounded runs, safe retries and range re-runs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-COMPUTE]{1}, [CAP-DELIVERY]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Declared jobs run on schedules and when data arrives, and each run is bounded, so backlogs drain on their own."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "A run with no limit either finishes early or is killed partway through, and neither tells you what the next run will do. Giving each run a budget, plus a final step that re-queues whatever is left, keeps work flowing without anyone triggering it by hand."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Job declarations in the product repository."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Triggers on a schedule, on file arrival and on completion of upstream work."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Re-runs over a range, with a limit on concurrency."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Set the cap for each run from the median time per item you've actually measured, not a configured guess. If the cap is missing, treat the run as uncapped, not as stopped."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Contract"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Clause"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Level"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Requirement"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "How conformance is shown"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Jobs are declared in the product's repository and deployed by CI."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "No job exists in an environment without a declaration in a repository."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Jobs can be triggered by schedule, by file arrival and by the completion of upstream work."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Each trigger type is exercised by a test job."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Each run has a budget. Work beyond the budget is re-triggered by a finishing step that re-queues only if work remains and the run made progress, and a run with nothing to do exits within seconds on the cheapest compute.{1}*Example:* A run may process 400 pages in its time budget; with 1,000 waiting, it processes 400 and re-queues itself, and the backlog drains without anyone triggering it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Feed more work than one budget allows; the backlog drains without manual triggers, and an empty run costs seconds."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Retries are safe because every task is idempotent; the orchestrator also rejects a duplicate run identifier."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Re-run a completed task; outputs are byte-identical."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "A job can be re-run for a declared range of partitions, with a limit on concurrent runs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Run a range backfill; only the declared partitions change."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "CAP-ORCHESTRATION.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Alerts fire on data freshness, not only on job failure."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-orchestration.md
msgid "Stop an upstream source; a freshness alert fires within its window."
msgstr ""

